From: Dirk Mueller <dmueller@suse.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/dtc: remove redundant YYLOC global declaration

Modern host compilers default to -fno-common. The parser already defines
and declares yylloc, so the lexer definition causes a multiple-definition
link failure. Remove the redundant definition instead of restoring the
old compiler behavior.

Upstream: https://git.kernel.org/linus/e33a814e772cdc36436c8c188d8c42d019fda639
Signed-off-by: Dirk Mueller <dmueller@suse.com>
Signed-off-by: David Gibson <david@gibson.dropbear.id.au>
Signed-off-by: Rob Herring <robh@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---
--- a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l
+++ b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l
@@ -38,7 +38,6 @@
 #include "srcpos.h"
 #include "dtc-parser.tab.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
 extern bool treesource_error;
 
 /* CAUTION: this will stop working if we ever use yyless() or yyunput() */
